data: {"type":"data-guide","id":"guide","data":{"slug":"gmail","permalink":"/guides/gmail","guide":{"verdict":{"tier":"review_required","summary":"Outside users trigger Google OAuth review when the public app requests sensitive, restricted, or user-data scopes. Internal apps limited to the developer's Workspace organization do not require verification.","effort_hours":{"min":1.0,"max":3.0},"calendar":{"min_days":14.0,"max_days":null,"label":"Google states verification can take several weeks."},"calendar_basis":"official","confidence":"high"},"situations":{"questions":[{"id":"audience","text":"Who will connect Gmail?","options":[{"id":"own_workspace","label":"Only my organization"},{"id":"outside_users","label":"Users outside my organization"},{"id":"mixed","label":"Both internal and external users"}]},{"id":"capability","text":"What must the agent do?","options":[{"id":"read","label":"Read Gmail data"},{"id":"write_send","label":"Write, modify, or send email"}]}],"variants":[{"when":{"audience":"own_workspace","capability":"read"},"tier":"instant","summary":"An internal app does not require verification and is accessible to users within the organization.","calendar_label":"No verification wait; implementation time is estimated.","notes":["Workspace administrators can still block the app."]},{"when":{"audience":"own_workspace","capability":"write_send"},"tier":"instant","summary":"An internal app does not require verification, even when the agent can modify Gmail data.","calendar_label":"No verification wait; implementation time is estimated.","notes":["Domain-wide Delegation can be configured for specified scopes."]},{"when":{"audience":"outside_users","capability":"read"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"A public external app requesting Gmail user-data scopes must complete verification before broad use.","calendar_label":"Google states that verification can take several weeks.","notes":["Testing-status access is limited by the applicable test-user rules."]},{"when":{"audience":"outside_users","capability":"write_send"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"A public external app requesting Gmail write or send permissions is subject to scope and brand verification.","calendar_label":"Google states that verification can take several weeks.","notes":["Use the narrowest non-sensitive scopes that provide the required Gmail capability."]}]},"byo_advice":"Composio's managed Gmail app is the fastest option when a separately registered Google OAuth client is unnecessary. To bring your own, sign in to Google Cloud, configure the OAuth consent screen and requested Gmail scopes, create the OAuth client and client credential, set Composio's callback URI as the allowed redirect URI, and paste the resulting client ID and secret into the Composio auth config.","before_you_start":[{"text":"The developer console needs a signed-in account: Sign-in page at accounts.google.com.","evidence":{"label":"TESTED","source_id":"s6","quote":null,"found_in":null,"note":"Our read-only probe on 2026-10-22 loaded https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview and ended at https://accounts.google.com/v3/signin/identifier?continue=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&followup=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&osid=1&passive=1209600&service=cloudconsole&flowName=GlifWebSignIn&flowEntry=ServiceLogin&dsh=S1377249577:1792655465416351 (login wall)."}},{"text":"Decide whether the app is Internal or External; Internal apps are limited to the developer's Workspace organization and do not require verification.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"All users within your organization can access. Verification is not required.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Identify the least-privilege Gmail scope for each required operation; exact Gmail scope strings are not present in the supplied claims.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"Many scopes overlap, so it's best to use a scope that isn't sensitive.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Collect the app name, logo, scope descriptions, and a concise explanation of how the agent uses Gmail data for consent and review.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"App name, logo, and scopes are shown on the consent screen without warnings (once brand and scopes are verified).","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Have a real Google Cloud project and developer account ready for app registration.","evidence":{"label":"UNCERTAIN","source_id":null,"quote":null,"found_in":null,"note":"The console sign-in wall establishes that a Google account is required, but the exact Gmail OAuth project prerequisites were not otherwise documented in the supplied claims."}},{"text":"Plan for possible several-week verification if the chosen scope category requires review.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"The Google\nOAuth app verification process can take several weeks","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"limits":[{"what":"Test users for an external app in Testing status","value":100.0,"unit":"test users","scope":"External apps in Testing status","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Only users explicitly added to the test user allowlist can access the app (limited to a hard cap of 100 test users).","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"Refresh-token expiration for Testing-status apps used by a Google Workspace organization with Trusted status","value":7.0,"unit":"days","scope":"Testing-status apps used by a Google Workspace organization with Trusted status","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"This\nstatus overrides certain standard OAuth limitations for the organization's users, such as\nthe 100-test-user cap and the 7-day refresh token expiration limit for apps in the\nTesting status.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"Total users for a published, unverified external app requesting sensitive or restricted scopes","value":100.0,"unit":"total users","scope":"Published external apps that are Unverified and request sensitive or restricted scopes","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"for apps requesting sensitive or restricted scopes, unverified app warnings (Danger UI) will be displayed to users, and a hard cap of 100 total users applies.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"Re-verification frequency for apps requesting restricted scopes","value":1.0,"unit":"year","scope":"Apps requesting restricted scopes data","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Apps requesting restricted scopes data need to complete “re-verification” annually.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"steps":[{"n":1,"title":"Sign in to Google Cloud","detail":"Sign in to the Google Cloud Console and open the OAuth app configuration area for a project you control.","actor":"human","human_reason":"credential","irreversible":false,"values":[],"evidence":{"label":"UNCERTAIN","source_id":null,"quote":null,"found_in":null,"note":"The supplied observation shows that console access redirects to the Google Accounts sign-in page; the exact project-selection flow was not verified."}},{"n":2,"title":"Register your own Gmail OAuth app","detail":"Create an OAuth application in the console. Set the user type to External for customers outside your organization and use Testing during development.","actor":"human","human_reason":"real_account","irreversible":false,"values":[{"label":"User type","value":"External"},{"label":"Publishing status","value":"Testing"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"These applications target the widest possible\naudience, including individual Google Account holders and users within external Google\nWorkspace organizations.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":3,"title":"Configure consent and minimum scopes","detail":"Select only the Gmail permissions required by the agent, describe the integration, and prepare the consent-screen brand and scope information. The exact Gmail scope strings were not verified in the supplied claims.","actor":"agent","human_reason":null,"irreversible":false,"values":[],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"Many scopes overlap, so it's best to use a scope that isn't sensitive.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":4,"title":"Add the Composio callback URL","detail":"Add Composio's callback as an allowed redirect URI. Use the exact value below in the provider's redirect field.","actor":"either","human_reason":null,"irreversible":false,"values":[{"label":"Redirect URI","value":"https://backend.composio.dev/api/v3/toolkits/auth/callback"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"--allowed-redirect-uris=\"REDIRECT_URI\"","found_in":"visible","note":"Google requires an allowed redirect URI; the callback value shown here is the required Composio callback."}},{"n":5,"title":"Create the OAuth client credential","detail":"Create a confidential OAuth client, then create its client credential and obtain the client ID and client secret. Keep the secret out of source control and logs.","actor":"human","human_reason":"credential","irreversible":false,"values":[],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"Create an OAuth client.\nCreate an OAuth client credential.\nIn the OAuth client credential, obtain the client secret.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":6,"title":"Configure the Composio authentication","detail":"Paste the newly issued client ID and client secret into Composio's own-provider Gmail auth configuration, and test the connection. Confirm the exact field names in the current Composio interface before saving.","actor":"human","human_reason":"credential","irreversible":false,"values":[],"evidence":{"label":"UNCERTAIN","source_id":null,"quote":null,"found_in":null,"note":"The supplied claims describe Google's OAuth client creation but do not document the current Composio BYO configuration fields."}},{"n":7,"title":"Move to production and obtain approval","detail":"For external use, transition the app to In production and submit the required brand and scope verification if the selected scopes require it. Google states that verification can take several weeks.","actor":"human","human_reason":"wait","irreversible":false,"values":[{"label":"Publishing status","value":"In production"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"Publishing status: Transition to In production.\nUser type: Set to External if your app serves customers outside your\norganization, such as advertiser clients.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"review":{"required":"conditional","trigger":"External or public users use an app requesting sensitive, restricted, or other user-data scopes; internal organization-only apps do not require verification.","submit":["Set the publishing status to Testing during development.","Use the External user type when serving customers outside the organization.","Request OAuth verification, including brand and scope verification when sensitive or restricted scopes are requested.","Transition the app to In production near launch.","Submit re-verification annually when restricted scopes are requested."],"reviewer":"Google","wait_official":"The Google OAuth app verification process can take several weeks.","wait_community":null,"cost":null,"evidence":[{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"The Google\nOAuth app verification process can take several weeks","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Required for public apps that request sensitive and restricted scopes.","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"Sensitive scopes require review by Google and have a\nsensitive indicator on the Google Cloud Console's OAuth consent screen configuration\npage.","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"All users within your organization can access. Verification is not required.","found_in":"visible","note":null}]},"customer_gates":[{"text":"A Google Workspace administrator has final authority over whether the app can access the organization's data.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"the Google Workspace administrator has the ultimate authority on whether an app can access their\norganization's data.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"A Workspace administrator can block the OAuth app regardless of its user type, publishing state, or verification state.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Block any OAuth app, whether it is Internal or External, Testing or\nPublished, or Verified or Unverified, preventing their users from authorizing it.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Domain-wide Delegation can be configured for specified scopes to bypass user consent, but administrator policy still applies.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Domain-wide Delegation\n(DWD) can also be configured to bypass user consent for specific scopes.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"A Testing-status external app normally allows only explicitly added test users, up to 100.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Only users explicitly added to the test user allowlist can access the app (limited to a hard cap of 100 test users).","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"gotchas":[{"text":"Testing-status apps that are not Trusted for a Workspace organization are subject to a seven-day refresh-token expiration limit.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"This\nstatus overrides certain standard OAuth limitations for the organization's users, such as\nthe 100-test-user cap and the 7-day refresh token expiration limit for apps in the\nTesting status.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"An unverified published external app requesting sensitive or restricted scopes can show warnings and has a hard cap of 100 total users.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"for apps requesting sensitive or restricted scopes, unverified app warnings (Danger UI) will be displayed to users, and a hard cap of 100 total users applies.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"If the client secret leaks, delete and recreate the client credential.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"If the client secret is\nleaked, you must delete and re-create the client credential.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Apps requesting restricted scopes must complete re-verification annually.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Apps requesting restricted scopes data need to complete “re-verification” annually.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Redirect URI registration is provider-specific; paste the Composio callback exactly and avoid substituting another callback.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"REDIRECT_URI: the redirect URI for the\nOAuth application—for example, https://myapp.com/signin-callback.","found_in":"visible","note":"The required Composio callback value is supplied in the registration step."}}],"blockers":[{"symptom":"Users see an \"unverified app\" warning during testing.","cause":"The app has not completed the required verification request.","fix":"Submit the verification request and wait for Google's review.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"If you see unverified\napp on the screen when testing your application, you must submit a\nverification request to remove it.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"symptom":"The client credential stops working after a secret exposure.","cause":"The client secret was leaked and is no longer considered safe.","fix":"Delete the exposed credential, create a replacement, and update the Composio auth configuration.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"If the client secret is\nleaked, you must delete and re-create the client credential.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"symptom":"External testing access stops at 100 users.","cause":"The app is in Testing and users are restricted to the test-user allowlist.","fix":"Add approved test users or complete the applicable production and verification process.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Only users explicitly added to the test user allowlist can access the app (limited to a hard cap of 100 test users).","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"prepared":{"scopes":[{"scope":"Gmail API scope for the exact read, send, modify, or delete operations required (exact scope string not verified)","why":"Gmail access cannot be reduced or classified until the agent's required actions are mapped to provider scopes.","review_class":"unknown"},{"scope":"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/userinfo.email","why":"Allows viewing the primary Google Account email address when account identification is required.","review_class":"sensitive"},{"scope":"openid, email, profile","why":"These are basic identity scopes that can support sign-in without a test-user allowlist when they are the only requested scopes.","review_class":"none"}],"privacy_policy_outline":["Identify the developer, the Gmail data accessed, and the agent use case.","Describe data retention, deletion, sharing, and user support procedures.","Explain that the connection is mediated through Composio."],"consent_screen":{"app_name":"[Developer product or agent name]","developer_contact":"[Verified developer or support contact]","purpose":"Use the requested Gmail permission to [specific agent action].","requested_permissions":"[Exact scope names and plain-language descriptions]"},"review_text":"The external app uses Composio to connect a user's Google account. It requests only the Gmail scopes required for [specific actions], displays the app name, logo, and scope descriptions on the consent screen, and includes privacy and support information."},"open_questions":["What exact Gmail API scopes are required for the intended read, send, create, update, and delete operations?","Will the app serve only the developer's Workspace organization, making it Internal, or external users, making it External?","Will the selected Gmail scopes be classified as non-sensitive, sensitive, or restricted?","What exact fields does the current Composio BYO Gmail auth configuration present for the client ID, secret, scopes, and callback?","What additional consent-screen, privacy-policy, demonstration, or reviewer contact materials does Google's current verification console require?"],"schema_version":"1","slug":"gmail","app_name":"Gmail","guide_type":"generated","last_verified":"2026-10-22","composio":{"toolkit_slug":"gmail","status":"managed","callback_url":"https://backend.composio.dev/api/v3/toolkits/auth/callback","callback_note":"Copy the exact redirect URI shown in your Composio auth config; some toolkits still show the legacy https://backend.composio.dev/api/v1/auth-apps/add."},"wall_probe":{"console_url":"https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview","final_url":"https://accounts.google.com/v3/signin/identifier?continue=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&followup=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&osid=1&passive=1209600&service=cloudconsole&flowName=GlifWebSignIn&flowEntry=ServiceLogin&dsh=S1377249577:1792655465416351","redirect_chain":["https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview","https://accounts.google.com/ServiceLogin?service=cloudconsole&passive=1209600&osid=1&continue=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&followup=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview","https://accounts.google.com/v3/signin/identifier?continue=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&followup=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&osid=1&passive=1209600&service=cloudconsole&flowName=GlifWebSignIn&flowEntry=ServiceLogin&dsh=S1377249577:1792655465416351"],"outcome":"login_wall","wall_host":"accounts.google.com","asks_for":"Sign-in page at accounts.google.com","bot_check":false,"method":"http","observed_at":"2026-10-22"},"conflicts":[],"sou